+# Independent IGS97 model review
+
+SCI-igs97-agent-v1, 2 November 2026. Actual separate reviewer `/root/maxwell_checklist_review`; I did not author the root transcription, the Cartesian oracle, the source audits, the integrator correction or the reports. Historical author-run identities were not recorded; I do not invent them. All nine items pass **only for the scope below**. This is a new decision under the current agent-review policy, not a retrospective acceptance of old pending reviews or an extension of TMD2 reporting approval.
+
+Exact candidate: models/hypoplastic-sand-igs97.json, SHA256 83777458ea437a3a7c1360117dbf435f7d763913cda399099ef2966e65a67e86. Schema0.1/draft metadata remain unchanged. The explicit v0.3 crosswalk is interpretive evidence, not a migration or acceptance of new bytes. Recorded HEAD is provenance context, not a clean-tree attestation.
+
+## Accepted scope
+
+The continuous NH97 history/stiffness overlay composed with the **general eight-physical-parameter VW96 host**, in compression-positive Mandel effective skeleton Cauchy stress, infinitesimal kinematics, fixed spatial frame and zero spin. Explicit complete sigma/e/h supplies the material state. Rates are per normalized strain-path fraction, not seconds. Symbolic source fidelity is assessed with the numerical conventions identified below; numerical verification is limited to the retained instantaneous cases, eight short prescribed-strain histories/15 increments and named hidden-crossing/transaction probes.
+
+Historical full numerical evidence is the native CLI evaluate/integrate identity 603f8829171fbaff697ba543787f62622e73f944fe25aa2bbe3fb189548e1443 in the v2 report. A separate retained common-runtime run supplies narrower crossing, five-cycle-increment and budget/rollback corroboration for its own native/Wasm artifacts, not a rerun of all303 cases. Ordinary laboratory run/control protocols, the research-quarter-strain interface, all current release/package/browser APIs, full tangents, FE integration and deployment are not qualified by this decision. Their availability or retained logs do not transfer numerical scope.
+
+The source physical history ball is norm(h)<=R. Compressive-soil applicability uses Decision0004's project restriction to strictly compressive principal effective stresses, positive pressure and strict interior ed<e<ei, including exact isotropy. The root accepts wider algebraic continuations. Its j2<=1e-24 Lode substitution, pressure cutoff, strict endpoints, rho cap and 1% band remain numerical choices. No all-stage confinement or continuum-wide accuracy is inferred from saved endpoints. Do not use the band as a physical initial condition or describe a trajectory as wholly inside the physical ball without actual stage coverage.
+
+The default host vector is p_ref=100000Pa (numerical scale), phi=pi/6, hs=5.8e9Pa, n=.28, ed0=.53, ec0=.84, ei0=1, alpha=.13, beta=1.05; IGS defaults R=1e-4,mR=5,mT=2,beta_r=.5,chi=6. Two additional rate-only IGS vectors are exactly those in the saved report. Exploratory mR=mT or chi=.5 cases verify code behavior, not NH97 parameter recommendations. No entire parameter box is approved.
+
+## source_provenance
+
+PASS. I checked the bytes of both user-supplied original PDFs and visually inspected the primary equation/sign/domain/algorithm pages, with precise coverage in source-reading.json. NH97 is the printed1997 paper, despite the filename1998 label: Niemunis and Herle, Mechanics of Cohesive-Frictional Materials2,279-299, DOI10.1002/(SICI)1099-1484(199710)2:4<279::AID-CFM29>3.0.CO;2-8. The1996 host is von Wolffersdorff, volume1,251-271, DOI10.1002/(SICI)1099-1484(199607)1:3<251::AID-CFM13>3.0.CO;2-3. Primary PDF hashes agree with original receipts. Relevant equations, not later web summaries, govern this decision. Existing complete audits supply broader reading context; I make no claim to have visually inspected every page of either article.
+
+The later numgeo continuous-law cross-check and inspected author update algorithm remain distinct from the primary identity. No supplied author binary/code was executed. This composition is not ISA, generalized IGS or a finite-spin implementation.
+
