+
+PASS with explicit numerical-variant labeling. NH97 Eqs7-8 define uncapped rho and history direction, including zero direction at zero history. Contracting Eq14 gives exactly the root positive-projection correction rho^chi*((1-mT)*L:eta+N)*(eta:D), and the nonpositive correction rho^chi*(mR-mT)*(L:eta)*(eta:D), added to the interpolated linear operator. Eq15 gives history loading/reversal branches. Both corrections vanish at zero projection; the stress rate is continuous there, but its derivative need not be. Zero history gives mR*L:D and h'=D; saturated aligned loading recovers the host, reversal mR*L:D and orthogonal loading mT*L:D. Equal multipliers alone do not remove arbitrary unsaturated-history effects.
+
+VW96 Eqs40-46 supply the root general linear/nonlinear tensors, friction/shape, pressure-dependent density bounds, density factors and fb normalization. NH97 AppendixA Eq29 has the combined (1+ei)/e density factor and equals that general host only at beta=1, because ei/ec=ei0/ec0. Current beta1.05, VW96TableI beta1.5 and the TMD2 later published beta2.5 are distinct identities. Root defaults are not NH97TableI. Void-ratio continuity is source VW96Eq2, sign-converted.
